.TH CDLOCKER 1 "October 2026" "ColDog Locker" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cdlocker \- manage encrypted ColDog Locker directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cdlocker
.RI [ command " [" arguments ]]
.br
.B cdlocker help
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B cdlocker --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cdlocker
manages password-protected locker directories through CLI commands, a graphical
interface and a terminal interface. With no arguments, it prints help.
.PP
An unlocked locker is an ordinary directory. Locking creates an authenticated,
encrypted archive, removes the plaintext source and publishes the archive as
.B locker.cdl
in a directory with a leading dot. Hidden/system attributes are applied where
supported. Unlocking authenticates the archive and restores the ordinary folder.
.PP
Locker registration and recovery records are stored in a per-user SQLite
database. Settings and logs use the same per-user data directory.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B gui
Launch the Avalonia graphical interface. Installed macOS packages open
.IR "/Applications/ColDog Locker.app" .
.TP
.BR tui ", " terminal
Launch the terminal user interface for essential locker operations.
.TP
.BI "new " "name " "[--path parent] [--password password]"
Create a locker. The path option selects its parent, not the final directory.
Without it, GUI, CLI and TUI creation use the saved
.B default-location
setting. Initially this is ColDog Locker under the platform documents folder,
falling back to the user profile when no documents folder is available.
.TP
.BI "lock " "name " "[--password password]"
Encrypt a locker. Prompts for its password unless supplied as an option.
An already locked locker is left unchanged and returns success.
.TP
.BI "unlock " "name " "[--password password]"
Authenticate and decrypt a locker. Prompts for its password unless supplied as
an option. An already unlocked locker is left unchanged and returns success.
.TP
.BR list " [--locked | --unlocked]"
Print known lockers, states and locations, optionally filtered by state.
.TP
.BI "status " name
Print state, path, GUID, timestamps and content counts. Incomplete content
inspection reports unavailable counts and returns failure.
.TP
.BI "verify " name
Check registration, directory access and content counts. For a locked locker,
also check archive header/registration agreement, recorded SHA-256 and unexpected
neighboring entries. This does not authenticate encrypted contents with a
password. Test a backup with
.B recover
into a new directory.
.TP
.BI "change-password " "name " "[--old-password password --new-password password]"
Change the password of an unlocked locker. An incorrect current password stops
the command before requesting or validating a replacement. Interactive changes
show all password requirements, then request a new password and confirmation.
If either password option is supplied, both are required. Older archive backups
still need their original password.
.TP
.BI "edit " "name " "[--name new-name] [--location existing-directory]"
Edit an unlocked registration without moving or renaming files. At least one
option is required. The existing directory leaf must match the selected name;
protected or overlapping paths are refused.
.TP
.BI "open " name
Open the registered location in the desktop file manager. Requires a graphical
desktop and an available file manager.
.TP
.BI "remove " "name " "[--force] [--delete]"
Remove an unlocked registration. Files remain unless
.B --delete
is supplied. Removal asks for confirmation unless
.B --force
is supplied. Locked lockers cannot be removed.
.TP
.BI "recover " "archive.cdl new-destination " "[--password password]"
Authenticate and extract a version 2 archive without loading the database.
The destination's parent must exist and the destination must be new. Preserves
the archive and never overwrites existing output. Does not register the restored
folder or resolve operation records. Enter the original archive password when
prompted. Version 1 archives are unsupported.
.TP
.B recovery-list
List unfinished operations and their source, target and staging paths. A record
can belong to an active process. After an interruption, preserve all listed
artifacts before choosing a recovery action.
.TP
.BI "recovery-cancel " operation-id
Cancel eligible interrupted preparation before source removal or publication
readiness. Requires the source to exist, the target to be absent and registration
to match. Preserves all files and moves the record to recovery history.
.TP
.BI "recovery-finish " operation-id
Verify output for an operation at MetadataCommitted and move the record to
history without changing files. Refuses missing or changed output. For an
unlock, the original archive need not still exist.
.TP
.BI "recovery-restore " "operation-id archive.cdl new-destination " "[--password password]"
Authenticate a retained archive, restore into a new directory and repair the
recorded operation's registration. The destination's parent must exist; its
leaf must match the original locker name. Choose an archive at the recorded
source path for unlock, or staging/target path for lock. Preserve original and
staging files, which may contain plaintext. Wrong passwords leave the operation
pending.
.TP
.B recovery-history
Show resolved operations, retained paths and recovery attempts. Does not delete
retained artifacts.
.TP
.BR settings " [key [value]]"
Show all settings, show one setting, or update one setting. See SETTINGS.
.TP
.B settings reset
Restore default settings without deleting registrations or locker contents.
.TP
.B db-info
Print database path, existence, size, timestamps, locker count, SQLite version
and integrity status.
.TP
.B db-vacuum
Optimize the SQLite database and update its last-vacuum timestamp.
.TP
.BI "db-backup " new-directory
Create a verified metadata snapshot at new-directory/lockers.db. The parent
must exist and the destination must be new. The backup contains names, paths,
password verifiers and recovery records; it is not encrypted and contains no
locker files. Back up archives/files separately and retain original passwords.
.TP
.BI "db-restore " backup-lockers.db
Restore a compatible snapshot only when the current registry and SQLite
sidecars are absent. Close other app instances first. Never replaces an existing
registry; do not delete a live registry to bypass this check. Ordinary
registrations need their original paths; pending operations retain their
recovery records. Preserves the input backup and changes no locker files.
.TP
.BR update " [--download]"
Check releases for the configured channel and platform and show release notes.
With the option, download and verify the matching installer. Windows starts
installation; macOS opens Installer. Linux removes the installed coldog-locker
package before installing the verified DEB/RPM through the package manager;
administrator approval may be required.
.TP
.B about
Show version, license and alphabetically sorted third-party acknowledgements.
Works without database initialization.
.TP
.B dev
Print diagnostic environment information, including the authoritative local
configuration path, runtime, architecture, free space and process memory.
.TP
.BR help " [command]"
Show general or command-specific help. Works without database initialization.
.TP
.BR --version ", " -v
Show semantic version, build identity with source revision and numeric assembly
version. Build date/time are not recorded. Works without database initialization.
.SH PASSWORDS
New passwords require at least 12 characters, an uppercase letter, a lowercase
letter, a digit and a special character. Blocked common words and sequential or
keyboard patterns are rejected. Passwords cannot be recovered if forgotten.
.PP
Prefer interactive prompts. Options
.BR --password ,
.B --old-password
and
.B --new-password
can expose passwords through shell history, scripts, logs or process listings.
The latter two options apply only to
.BR change-password .
.PP
The GUI checks the current password first, then shows new password,
confirmation and live requirements together. Change Password remains disabled
until the rules pass and both fields match. Show password reveals both fields;
both fields are cleared on close.
.SH LOCKER NAMES
A name must be a valid single filename on the current platform, not an absolute
path, a relative path, dot or dot-dot. Unicode, interior spaces and supported
punctuation are accepted. Quote names containing spaces or shell metacharacters
when typing commands in a shell; platform filename restrictions still apply.
.SH SETTINGS
.TP
.B default-location
Safe parent directory for future lockers. Does not move existing lockers.
.TP
.B theme
GUI theme: auto, light, dark or cds.
.TP
.B view
Default GUI view: grid or list.
.TP
.BR debug ", " file-logging ", " auto-update
Boolean values: true or false.
.TP
.B log-level
One of debug, info, warning, error or fatal.
.TP
.B log-format
One of json or text.
.TP
.B max-file-size
Log rotation size in MB, from 1 to 1024.
.TP
.B update-channel
One of stable (s), unstable (u) or prerelease (pre, p).
.TP
.B db-vacuum-interval
Stored interval preference in days, from 0 to 365. This build does not schedule
automatic vacuum operations; run db-vacuum explicitly.
.SH FILES
The per-user data directory contains settings.json, lockers.db and logs/.
.TP
.B Linux
${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/ColDog Studios/ColDog Locker
.TP
.B macOS
$HOME/Library/Application Support/ColDog Studios/ColDog Locker
.TP
.B Windows
%LOCALAPPDATA%\eColDog Studios\eColDog Locker
.PP
Run
.B cdlocker dev
for the authoritative path on the current account.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B COLDOG_LOCKER_DATA_HOME
Absolute base-directory override for application data. The application appends
ColDog Studios/ColDog Locker beneath this base. Relative values are refused.
.SH OUTPUT
Standard output and error messages use UTF-8 without a byte-order mark,
including redirected output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including an already locked/unlocked locker that needed no change.
.TP
.B 1
Error.
.TP
.B 2
Update available but no downloadable installer is available for this platform.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
cdlocker new "Private café" --path "$HOME/Private"
cdlocker lock "Private café"
cdlocker unlock "Private café"
cdlocker change-password "Private café"
cdlocker list --locked
cdlocker verify "Private café"
cdlocker settings update-channel stable
cdlocker settings theme dark
cdlocker about
cdlocker recovery-list
cdlocker recover "/backup/locker.cdl" "$HOME/RecoveredLocker"
cdlocker update
.EE
.SH SECURITY NOTES
This is prerelease software. Keep independent, tested backups and close writers
or folder synchronization before locking. Ordinary local filesystems are the
supported storage target; network/cloud/removable storage has no portable
atomicity or power-loss recovery guarantee.
.PP
Detected concurrent changes abort locking, but retained native writable handles
and interrupted operations can still cause data loss. Locking removes ordinary
plaintext files; it does not securely erase deleted blocks, snapshots or backups.
System paths, drive roots, profile roots and top-level user folders are blocked.
.PP
After an interruption, preserve all reported paths and use the recovery
commands. Do not delete operation records or artifacts to force a retry.
.PP
Windows and macOS installers are unsigned; platform security warnings may occur.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation and backup/recovery instructions:
.I https://github.com/ColDog-Studios/ColDog-Locker/tree/main/docs
